1
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:18,920
It worked fine just last night.

2
00:00:19,739 --> 00:00:20,120
It's fine.

3
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:21,600
It's just a loose connection.

4
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:22,280
There, all fixed.

5
00:00:28,079 --> 00:00:28,940
Zhuzi's back.

6
00:00:31,359 --> 00:00:32,060
Hello, Uncle.

7
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:37,979
Why were you out all night?

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,740
Just back from the hospital with Haizhu.

9
00:00:43,119 --> 00:00:43,600
The hospital?

10
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:44,920
Did you... get into a fight?

11
00:00:45,579 --> 00:00:47,179
Out playing the hero for justice again?

12
00:00:47,479 --> 00:00:48,320
No, Uncle.

13
00:00:48,679 --> 00:00:50,380
A bunch of punks picked a fight.

14
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,920
Haizhu beat them and chased them off.

15
00:00:52,119 --> 00:00:53,420
Isn't that still getting into a fight?

16
00:00:54,119 --> 00:00:55,719
No, the punks went after him

17
00:00:55,899 --> 00:00:57,920
because he stepped in at their dance hall.

18
00:00:58,380 --> 00:00:59,020
A dance hall?

19
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,100
What were you doing at a dance hall?

20
00:01:01,179 --> 00:01:02,659
That place is nothing but trouble!

21
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:03,939
Uncle,

22
00:01:04,159 --> 00:01:05,959
I have to explain this from the start.

23
00:01:06,359 --> 00:01:07,760
Remember when Haizhu went to the station

24
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:08,719
and got locked up for two days?

25
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:10,040
Hold on, wait a second.

26
00:01:11,079 --> 00:01:13,219
When did he end up in the lockup again?

27
00:01:13,379 --> 00:01:13,859
Old Liu, when was this?

28
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:15,219
You can't hit the kid!

29
00:01:15,359 --> 00:01:15,939
Don't hit him!

30
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:17,340
When did I ever hit him?

31
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:17,859
No, look.

32
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:19,700
The thugs in our area are saying

33
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,480
this kid's really made a name for himself.

34
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:23,200
He's a big shot in the city.

35
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:24,219
He even rules the turf now!

36
00:01:35,739 --> 00:01:36,579
What are you doing?

37
00:01:36,799 --> 00:01:38,239
Let me see how he rules the turf!

38
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,000
He's all grown up!

39
00:01:39,079 --> 00:01:40,260
Don't hit him, don't hit him!

40
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,000
No, wait...

41
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,280
None of you hold me back!

42
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:43,500
I'm gonna ask him how—

43
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,599
I'm asking how he rules the turf!

44
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:46,959
Calm down, calm down!

45
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:47,700
You can't hit him! Wait—

46
00:01:47,739 --> 00:01:48,400
No, I—

47
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,019
I'm asking how he rules the turf!

48
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:51,260
I've gotta ask him!

49
00:01:51,599 --> 00:01:53,739
If I don't hit him, he won't talk!

50
00:02:07,379 --> 00:02:08,000
Brother Batian.

51
00:02:08,699 --> 00:02:10,840
You comfortable staying at my place?

52
00:02:13,879 --> 00:02:14,879
Your place?

53
00:02:15,639 --> 00:02:16,300
Boss Zhang,

54
00:02:17,439 --> 00:02:19,460
that's ancient history.

55
00:02:22,099 --> 00:02:23,060
Look at that shot.

56
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:30,840
That was downright ugly.

57
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:34,879
Not bad.

58
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:40,379
That Liu Haizhu is your brother, right?

59
00:02:42,219 --> 00:02:43,400
Yeah, my brother.

60
00:02:45,419 --> 00:02:46,180
I knew it.

61
00:02:47,159 --> 00:02:48,180
Around Songliao,

62
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:49,460
in all my years out here,

63
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:50,780
I've only ever seen two guys

64
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:53,479
who refuse to play by the rules.

65
00:02:54,219 --> 00:02:55,520
And you two actually teamed up.

66
00:02:56,039 --> 00:02:56,759
That's great.

67
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:57,960
Both destined for big things.

68
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:03,479
Pulling seniority, huh?

69
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:06,139
The big shots who used to do that...

70
00:03:07,099 --> 00:03:07,699
are all gone.

71
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:19,560
Brother Batian,

72
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:21,860
since I came all the way here today,

73
00:03:22,719 --> 00:03:24,180
I'll cut straight to the chase.

74
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:25,780
Lately,

75
00:03:26,159 --> 00:03:28,419
our crews have been clashing pretty hard.

76
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:30,139
Still, I feel like we could...

77
00:03:31,719 --> 00:03:33,020
we could each take a step back.

78
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,300
How about we just stay in our own lanes?

79
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:38,919
Besides, out on the streets right now,

80
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,199
there are a lot of Uniformed cops around.

81
00:03:40,479 --> 00:03:41,560
If one of these days, by bad luck,

82
00:03:42,139 --> 00:03:43,680
they haul in one of your boys,

83
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:45,460
and make an example out of him,

84
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:47,719
what're you gonna do then?

85
00:03:52,539 --> 00:03:53,919
Songliao, this place,

86
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:56,020
is just one big river.

87
00:03:56,919 --> 00:03:59,319
There's no staying in our own lanes.

88
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:01,560
If that's how you're gonna talk,

89
00:04:01,759 --> 00:04:02,680
then we've got nothing to discuss.

90
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:04,379
There's plenty to discuss.

91
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:07,560
We'll talk with this.

92
00:04:12,379 --> 00:04:13,039
And another thing.

93
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,199
You said the cops are watching closely

94
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:16,959
and told us to keep our heads down.

95
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:19,019
Sounds to me like

96
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,000
you're up to something,

97
00:04:21,779 --> 00:04:23,000
and you're scared of being caught.

98
00:04:32,759 --> 00:04:34,240
Oh, my dear Brother Batian...

99
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,639
In a place like Songliao,

100
00:04:36,759 --> 00:04:38,740
if I'm locked up today, I'm out tomorrow.

101
00:04:39,819 --> 00:04:40,560
But as for you, Brother Batian,

102
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:41,779
you might not be so lucky.

103
00:04:42,579 --> 00:04:44,500
You're overstepping your bounds.

104
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,220
You crippled Huoyazi.

105
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:49,079
You ran Li Laogunzi out of town.

106
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:51,100
You took out Sun Biao, too.

107
00:04:51,740 --> 00:04:52,639
What's your game?

108
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:55,800
Think the food in the east isn't enough,

109
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:58,680
so you want the whole feast in Songliao?

110
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,019
That's right.

111
00:05:10,660 --> 00:05:12,939
Now you're pushing it way too far.

112
00:05:13,879 --> 00:05:15,079
When I started running these streets,

113
00:05:15,199 --> 00:05:16,480
you were still in diapers!

114
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:19,680
You're just a few years older,

115
00:05:20,079 --> 00:05:21,839
don't act like everyone's granddaddy.

116
00:05:22,459 --> 00:05:22,959
You

117
00:05:23,860 --> 00:05:25,579
have no right to lay down terms with me.

118
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:35,600
This way.

119
00:05:39,180 --> 00:05:40,720
Leaving already, Boss Zhang?

120
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:45,800
Want some frozen pear to cool off?

121
00:05:46,319 --> 00:05:47,779
Cool off, my ass! You disgust me.

122
00:05:59,079 --> 00:05:59,680
Brother Ziwen.

123
00:06:00,459 --> 00:06:01,040
How'd the talk go?

124
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,620
Told us to lay low.

125
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:05,699
Interesting.

126
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:07,980
What do you mean, bro?

127
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,319
They scared of the cops?

128
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,120
Fearing the cops is the result,

129
00:06:11,579 --> 00:06:12,240
not the reason.

130
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:14,579
You mean...

131
00:06:15,079 --> 00:06:15,959
they're planning something big?

132
00:06:17,819 --> 00:06:18,899
Well, I heard

133
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,620
he was pretty tight with Director Zhu

134
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:21,360
from the tractor plant.

135
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:26,980
Those bastards stole the supplies!

136
00:06:27,399 --> 00:06:29,220
No wonder they stopped fighting for turf.

137
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:30,879
They've got their eyes on a huge score.

138
00:06:42,399 --> 00:06:42,920
Comrade Officer,

139
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,120
as a matter of routine,

140
00:06:45,379 --> 00:06:46,660
around this time at year's end,

141
00:06:47,079 --> 00:06:49,860
we take full inventory of the factory.

142
00:06:51,399 --> 00:06:52,379
During the inventory, we found that

143
00:06:52,879 --> 00:06:54,439
standard supplies are all in order,

144
00:06:55,180 --> 00:06:57,920
but there's a newly imported shipment—

145
00:06:58,060 --> 00:07:00,199
of core parts for special marine engines.

146
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:02,639
I'm not exaggerating when I say,

147
00:07:03,399 --> 00:07:04,980
there are only a few in the Northeast.

148
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,720
They're worth millions.

149
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,519
So securing these components

150
00:07:11,759 --> 00:07:14,060
is our factory's top priority right now.

151
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,000
All right.

152
00:07:15,019 --> 00:07:16,740
Tell us the basics,

153
00:07:16,839 --> 00:07:17,680
and we'll see how we can assist.

154
00:07:18,459 --> 00:07:19,439
Here's the situation.

155
00:07:19,779 --> 00:07:21,519
The components have reached the dock.

156
00:07:21,699 --> 00:07:22,980
We've assigned our security section,

157
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:24,079
doubled the guard posts,

158
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:25,379
and set up 24-hour patrols.

159
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:26,980
They're our best men,

160
00:07:27,339 --> 00:07:28,040
so nothing should go wrong.

161
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:28,500
And yet...

162
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:29,839
well, the thing is...

163
00:07:30,439 --> 00:07:33,579
There are bound to be some issues.

164
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:36,060
The problem lies in...

165
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:37,300
It's that...

166
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:38,980
The dock is quite remote,

167
00:07:39,899 --> 00:07:40,860
and there's heavy foot traffic.

168
00:07:41,259 --> 00:07:42,040
It's hard to control.

169
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:43,980
On top of that,

170
00:07:44,379 --> 00:07:45,920
the manpower of our factory security

171
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:47,779
is fairly limited,

172
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:48,500
right?

173
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:49,800
Right, right, right.

174
00:07:50,279 --> 00:07:51,699
Right, right, right.

175
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:55,019
So we're still feeling uneasy,

176
00:07:55,439 --> 00:07:57,600
and would like the police to back us up.

177
00:07:58,579 --> 00:07:59,000
All right.

178
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:01,240
Don't worry, Director Ma.

179
00:08:01,639 --> 00:08:03,660
Protecting state property is our duty.

180
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:04,939
Shortly,

181
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,160
we'll talk to

182
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:08,139
the officers in charge of the dock area,

183
00:08:08,639 --> 00:08:09,519
and deploy some forces there.

184
00:08:10,439 --> 00:08:11,000
After that,

185
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:12,839
let's stay in touch if anything happens.

186
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:13,920
All right? Keep in touch.

187
00:08:14,439 --> 00:08:14,899
Wonderful.

188
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:16,100
Great.

189
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:17,759
On behalf of the whole factory,

190
00:08:18,319 --> 00:08:19,199
thank you, Comrade Officer.

191
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:20,199
Thank you.

192
00:08:20,639 --> 00:08:21,079
Just doing our job.

193
00:08:21,319 --> 00:08:21,779
Thanks again.

194
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,100
We'll head out now.

195
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:27,339
Let's see them out.

196
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,160
See them out, see them out.

197
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,080
Thank you so much.

198
00:08:34,019 --> 00:08:34,799
Much appreciated.

199
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:43,379
Is... is your back feeling any better?

200
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:45,179
Much better.

201
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:47,179
You should still take it easy.

202
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:50,179
You don't need to stay here with me.

203
00:08:50,279 --> 00:08:50,940
Go get some rest.

204
00:08:51,899 --> 00:08:53,840
This is my workshop. I like it here.

205
00:08:54,559 --> 00:08:55,519
Try this one.

206
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:02,840
Hold up, everyone! Put down your tools.

207
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:07,399
On behalf of the factory director,

208
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:09,080
I'm announcing the Spring Festival rules

209
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:10,179
and the work schedule.

210
00:09:11,279 --> 00:09:12,299
Our motor squad...

211
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,039
needs to see this final shift through,

212
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:17,200
so everyone can enjoy a peaceful New Year.

213
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:19,820
Also,

214
00:09:19,919 --> 00:09:21,299
there's an urgent shipment New Year's Day.

215
00:09:22,179 --> 00:09:24,820
The plant's assigning Comrade Zhou Meng

216
00:09:25,799 --> 00:09:26,960
to make a haul to the next county.

217
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:28,799
Loading is on New Year's Eve.

218
00:09:29,179 --> 00:09:30,919
Whoever's on shift takes responsibility.

219
00:09:31,539 --> 00:09:32,320
Keep a sharp eye on it!

220
00:09:32,539 --> 00:09:32,919
All right.

221
00:09:33,279 --> 00:09:34,080
Back to work, everyone.

222
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:34,980
Off you go.

223
00:09:35,519 --> 00:09:36,620
Wait, hold on!

224
00:09:37,639 --> 00:09:39,320
My request to visit family in Shanghai...

225
00:09:39,399 --> 00:09:40,340
was submitted long ago,

226
00:09:40,659 --> 00:09:41,980
and it's already been approved!

227
00:09:42,639 --> 00:09:45,019
My parents are waiting for me back home!

228
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,120
What's the matter?

229
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:49,159
Got an issue with management's assignment?

230
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:50,580
No,

231
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:52,500
I followed procedure to request time off,

232
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:54,580
and applied for family leave by the book!

233
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:55,799
Zhou Meng,

234
00:09:56,299 --> 00:09:57,840
you're an outstanding worker here.

235
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:00,759
The more critical the moment,

236
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:02,159
the more you need to step up

237
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:03,740
and set an example.

238
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:05,700
Didn't you tell me yourself?

239
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,139
Your place...

240
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:09,200
is right here in the garage.

241
00:10:10,759 --> 00:10:11,960
Just because I didn't give in to you,

242
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:13,840
you're purposely blocking my leave!

243
00:10:14,759 --> 00:10:15,500
Comrade Zhou Meng!

244
00:10:16,519 --> 00:10:17,919
Watch your mouth!

245
00:10:18,419 --> 00:10:20,539
The leadership puts full trust in you.

246
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:22,559
Trust?

247
00:10:23,899 --> 00:10:25,460
This is blatant retaliation!

248
00:10:26,039 --> 00:10:26,600
Comrade Zhou Meng,

249
00:10:27,379 --> 00:10:28,559
don't throw wild accusations around.

250
00:10:28,759 --> 00:10:29,980
This is work assigned by the factory.

251
00:10:30,179 --> 00:10:31,220
How is it retaliation?

252
00:10:32,779 --> 00:10:33,240
Come on.

253
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:36,399
What assignment comes up this last-minute?

254
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,860
And you're sending her out all alone?

255
00:10:37,919 --> 00:10:38,960
Seriously, what are you pulling?

256
00:10:39,659 --> 00:10:40,159
Hey, Liu Haizhu.

257
00:10:40,279 --> 00:10:42,179
Never learn your lesson, do you?

258
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:43,899
Back to your old tricks,

259
00:10:44,460 --> 00:10:46,340
driving a wedge between cadres and staff?

260
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,139
Aren't you supposed to be a model worker?

261
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:52,460
A great craftsman living by his skill?

262
00:10:53,659 --> 00:10:54,559
So when duty calls,

263
00:10:54,879 --> 00:10:56,340
you put yourself before the collective?

264
00:10:56,419 --> 00:10:57,379
What collective? You're just—

265
00:10:57,379 --> 00:10:57,960
Forget it.

266
00:11:01,019 --> 00:11:01,559
Fine.

267
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:03,299
Understood.

268
00:11:04,460 --> 00:11:05,740
I'll obey management's orders.

269
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:15,039
Don't worry.

270
00:11:16,139 --> 00:11:17,399
I'll work the New Year's Eve shift too,

271
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:20,000
and go to the next county with you.

272
00:11:46,059 --> 00:11:47,120
With New Year approaching,

273
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:48,740
the factory management reminds everyone

274
00:11:48,879 --> 00:11:50,299
to prioritize workplace safety

275
00:11:50,620 --> 00:11:51,740
and guard against fire and theft.

276
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:55,100
Check all equipment power before leaving.

277
00:11:55,559 --> 00:11:58,700
Staff on New Year's Eve must stay alert.

278
00:12:05,639 --> 00:12:06,600
Exactly.

279
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:09,299
Take these nice clothes home with you.

280
00:12:09,740 --> 00:12:11,000
Dress sharp,

281
00:12:11,139 --> 00:12:13,679
to show you're doing well in Songliao.

282
00:12:15,139 --> 00:12:16,460
Especially on New Year's Eve,

283
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:18,320
you should cook the reunion dinner.

284
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:20,179
Don't worry if it's not great.

285
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,500
The taste doesn't matter.

286
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:23,799
Your parents only care about the thought.

287
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:25,159
All right.

288
00:12:25,899 --> 00:12:26,360
Oh, right.

289
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:29,620
These are wood ear mushrooms.

290
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:31,500
You can stir-fry or stew them.

291
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:33,679
These are wild mountain mushrooms.

292
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:35,240
They make delicious soup.

293
00:12:35,679 --> 00:12:36,840
And this sachima,

294
00:12:36,919 --> 00:12:37,759
pastries and snacks.

295
00:12:37,860 --> 00:12:39,000
Take them home for your parents to try.

296
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:41,120
Mengmeng,

297
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:43,019
weren't these originally meant

298
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,700
for you to take home?

299
00:12:47,279 --> 00:12:49,379
Aren't these gifts meant for parents?

300
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:51,379
If you take them home,

301
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,379
it's like my thought is conveyed too.

302
00:12:53,919 --> 00:12:54,299
It's the same.

303
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:58,980
You've only been fussing over me.

304
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:00,899
How are you spending the New Year?

305
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:04,399
New Year? It's just another day.

306
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:07,919
Just eat and sleep.

307
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:09,720
You blink,

308
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:10,700
and it's over.

309
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:12,360
How is that the same?

310
00:13:13,299 --> 00:13:15,860
You only get one chance a year to go home,

311
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:16,879
and yet you...

312
00:13:21,899 --> 00:13:22,320
Dad,

313
00:13:22,860 --> 00:13:23,820
there's something I want to tell you.

314
00:13:24,639 --> 00:13:25,679
On New Year's Eve,

315
00:13:25,759 --> 00:13:27,120
I want to spend it with Zhou Meng.

316
00:13:31,559 --> 00:13:32,539
That's great!

317
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:36,480
Then I'll whip up at least eight dishes!

318
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:38,320
We'll invite Auntie Cai over too.

319
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:40,539
I meant...

320
00:13:41,039 --> 00:13:42,360
I'm going over to spend it with her.

321
00:13:44,519 --> 00:13:45,120
It's New Year.

322
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:46,960
Why go running around outside?

323
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:49,100
Zhou Meng is on duty on New Year's Eve.

324
00:13:49,179 --> 00:13:50,019
She'll be all by herself.

325
00:13:50,179 --> 00:13:51,100
I'm going to keep her company.

326
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:58,379
Well... all right then.

327
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:01,639
You young folks together...

328
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:02,100
Well,

329
00:14:03,379 --> 00:14:04,179
be careful.

330
00:14:04,379 --> 00:14:05,000
Don't, you know...

331
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:08,200
What? What are you thinking?

332
00:14:08,919 --> 00:14:10,740
What did I think? Nothing!

333
00:14:11,299 --> 00:14:12,659
You're not getting any younger.

334
00:14:13,039 --> 00:14:14,279
At my age,

335
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:16,360
worrying about the family line...

336
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,980
What's wrong with that?

337
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:19,440
Fine, just hurry up and paste it.

338
00:14:19,620 --> 00:14:20,059
Here.

339
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:22,399
Spread a bit more.

340
00:14:26,139 --> 00:14:26,539
That's enough.

341
00:14:27,539 --> 00:14:27,940
Listen,

342
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:29,460
I'll stew some meat later.

343
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:31,620
Take it over to the girl.

344
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:32,740
It's New Year.

345
00:14:32,799 --> 00:14:34,120
Don't let her feel neglected.

346
00:14:35,539 --> 00:14:36,580
Got it, don't worry.

347
00:14:37,019 --> 00:14:38,399
Even if you are, she won't be.

348
00:14:40,860 --> 00:14:41,580
What the hell are you talking about?

349
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:43,620
You little brat!

350
00:14:45,879 --> 00:14:46,440
Chip off the old block.
